target: internal/push/push.go
verify: go test ./internal/push/ -count=1 -run 'TestCheckReadsOmittedBranchesFromGit'
expect: were overridden by git
why:    git is the FALLBACK for an omitted flag, not an override. A caller that names the branch — Step 14 passes --branch — states which branch is being pushed, and reading git instead answers for whatever happens to be checked out in -repo, which is a different question when the two differ.
--- old
	if branch == "" {
		branch = currentBranch(p.Repo)
--- new
	if true {
		branch = currentBranch(p.Repo)
